// A chord ROW above the SECOND system of a staff that carries a `@rit` text spanner.
// The row has to clear the printed word, and on system 1 it did: the room merges the
// spanner into the staff's UP profile. A row above a LATER system is placed by the
// loose-line chain instead, which measured the INSIDE silhouette -- and an outside-staff
// grob is not in that -- so the same book printed the row clear of `rit.` on the first
// system and straight through it on the second (reported twice by a reader: 2026-08-28
// and 2026-08-29, scratch/ベースタブLy/Untitled-6.lys).
//
// The lyrics row is load-bearing, not decoration: without it both systems' rows come out
// of the room and the defect does not appear. Two sections rather than one played twice,
// so that nothing here depends on a section being replayed -- it never did.
title "Chord row over rit., second system"
key g major

part melody {
  section A { c4@rit c g' g | a@!rit a g2 | f4 f e e | d d c2 | break }
  section C { c4@rit c g' g | a@!rit a g2 | f4 f e e | d d c2 | break }
}

chords prog {
  section A { Dmaj7 | Em7 | Gmaj7 | A7 }
  section C { Dmaj7 | Em7 | Gmaj7 | A7 }
}

lyrics verse {
  section A { Twin- kle twin- kle | lit- tle star | How I won- der | what you are | }
  section C { Twin- kle twin- kle | lit- tle star | How I won- der | what you are | }
}

form main { A C }

score main "chordrow-rit-second-system" {
  chords prog as names
  staff melody
  lyrics verse sings melody
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// ⚠️ THIS NOTE IS AT THE FILE END ON PURPOSE. A comment ABOVE the music shifts every
// source offset after it, so the whole book's data-pos moves and its snapshot has to be
// re-based -- a diff that proves nothing and hides the next real one.
// ✔ VERIFIED TO GUARD, not assumed to (session 286): dropping the spanner merge from
// LayoutEngine.Rows.LeadingLinesOfSystem -- the defect this book was written for -- moves
// this snapshot (system 2's chord row falls from 3.40 staff spaces above the staff to
// 1.50, which is 0.49 above the `rit.` baseline) and moves NO other snapshot, which is
// why it had to be written: the whole 1519-book sweep moved ONE book, and that book is
// the reader's, not the repository's.
